{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מחוץ לפרכת העדות", :translit "mechutz laparochet ha'edut", :gloss "outside the curtain of the testimony"} {:he "אשר על העדות", :translit "asher al ha'edut", :gloss "which is over the testimony"} {:he "שנר מערבי הוא עדות ששכינה בישראל", :translit "she'ner ma'aravi hu edut she-shekhinah be'yisra'el", :gloss "that the western lamp is a testimony that the Shekhinah is among Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Two verses both link the menorah to the 'Testimony' — Exodus 27:21 says it is kindled 'over the Testimony,' and here it is placed 'outside the curtain of the Testimony.'"}], :frame {:text "The western lamp of the menorah burned miraculously longer than the others, testifying that God's presence dwells among Israel. This is stated explicitly at Shabbat 22b and Menachot 86b, and is derived from the verse Exodus 27:21 'over the Testimony' — the word 'testimony' signals that the lamp itself serves as ongoing witness.", :sources ["Shabbat 22b" "Menachot 86b" "Exodus 27:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מחוץ לפרכת", :translit "mechutz laparochet", :gloss "outside the curtain"} {:he "מ", :translit "mem", :gloss "mem"} {:he "מ", :translit "mem", :gloss "mem"} {:he "ההיכל הי' ארכו מ' אמה", :translit "ha-heikhal hayah archo mem amah", :gloss "the Hall its length was forty cubits"} {:he "הפרוכת הי' מדתה מ", :translit "ha-parochet hayah midatah mem", :gloss "the curtain its measure was forty"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word begins and ends with mem; mem has numerical value 40."}], :frame {:text "The Heikhal measured forty cubits in length, as stated at Yoma 15a and Middot 4:7. Ba'al HaTurim reads the mem at both ends of the word 'מחוץ' as a built-in mnemonic: mem equals forty, the measurement of the Hall and of the curtain.", :sources ["Yoma 15a" "Mishnah Middot 4:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יערוך אותו אהרן", :translit "ya'aroch oto aharon", :gloss "Aaron shall arrange it"} {:he "אהרן ובניו", :translit "aharon uvanav", :gloss "Aaron and his sons"} {:he "נדב ואביהוא", :translit "nadav va'avihu", :gloss "Nadav and Avihu"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between verses that say only 'Aaron' and verses that say 'Aaron and his sons' resolved by narrative of what Aaron did after Nadav and Avihu died."}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 10:1-2 records that Nadav and Avihu died when they offered unauthorized fire inside the Sanctuary. The Torah exempts Aaron and his sons from the obligation to mourn so they could continue the Tabernacle service (Leviticus 10:6-7). Yoma 53a relates that the High Priest alone enters the Holy of Holies for the incense service on Yom Kippur; Ba'al HaTurim reads the variant phrasing — 'Aaron' alone versus 'Aaron and his sons' (Exodus 27:21, Leviticus 24:3-4) — as reflecting Aaron's own practice after the death of his sons: he would accompany his remaining sons into the Hall but withdraw during the incense burning.", :sources ["Leviticus 10:1-2" "Leviticus 10:6-7" "Yoma 53a" "Exodus 27:21"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Two verses both link the menorah to the 'Testimony' — Exodus 27:21 says it is kindled 'over the Testimony,' and here it is placed 'outside the curtain of the Testimony.'", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Word begins and ends with mem; mem has numerical value 40.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast between verses that say only 'Aaron' and verses that say 'Aaron and his sons' resolved by narrative of what Aaron did after Nadav and Avihu died.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:25.360767495Z", :model "glm-5.2"}